        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Anatomy of an Active Black Hole — Infographic</title>\n<script id=\"MathJax-script\" async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    background: #111;\n    font-family: \"Trebuchet MS\", \"Segoe UI\", Arial, sans-serif;\n    color: #fff;\n  }\n  .page {\n    width: 593px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    background: #000;\n  }\n  /* ---------- NASA header ---------- */\n  .header {\n    background: #000;\n    height: 42px;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    padding: 4px 8px;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #222;\n  }\n  .nasa-logo {\n    width: 44px; height: 26px;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    background: #0b3d91;\n    color: #fff;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n    margin-right: 8px;\n  }\n  .jpl-text { line-height: 1.15; }\n  .jpl-text .l1 { font-size: 11px; }\n  .jpl-text .l2 { font-size: 8px; color: #cfd6e6; }\n\n  /* ---------- generic section ---------- */\n  section { position: relative; padding: 10px 14px 14px 14px; }\n  h2 {\n    margin: 4px 0 6px 4px;\n    font-size: 21px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    letter-spacing: 0.2px;\n  }\n  .caption { font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.45; }\n  .center { text-align: center; }\n\n  .placeholder {\n    background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,#2a2a35,#2a2a35 6px,#33333f 6px,#33333f 12px);\n    border: 1px dashed #8f8fa5;\n    color: #e6e6f0;\n    font-size: 9px;\n    font-style: italic;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 2px;\n  }\n  .circle { border-radius: 50%; }\n\n  /* ---------- Section 1 ---------- */\n  .s1 { background: linear-gradient(180deg,#3a1a52 0%, #2d1444 100%); height: 345px; }\n  .s1 .stage { position: relative; height: 250px; }\n  .s1 .lbl { position: absolute; text-align: center; font-size: 10.5px; line-height: 1.35; }\n  .s1 .lbl b { font-weight: bold; }\n  .s1 .lbl i { font-style: italic; }\n  .s1 .bottom { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }\n  .s1 .bottom div { width: 195px; }\n\n  /* ---------- Section 2 ---------- */\n  .s2 { background: linear-gradient(180deg,#6b3b0d 0%, #4a2708 100%); height: 285px; }\n  .s2 .row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; }\n  .s2 .mid { width: 155px; text-align: center; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.4; padding-top: 30px; }\n  .s2 .caps { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 8px; }\n  .s2 .caps div { width: 225px; text-align: center; }\n\n  /* ---------- Section 3 ---------- */\n  .s3 { background: #0e2a55; height: 285px; position: relative; }\n  .s3 .field { position: relative; height: 235px; }\n  .s3 .obj { position: absolute; }\n  .s3 .textmid {\n    position: absolute; left: 155px; top: 88px; width: 285px;\n    text-align: center; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45; z-index: 5;\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- Section 4 ---------- */\n  .s4 { background: #0f3d33; padding-bottom: 18px; }\n  .s4 .cols { display: flex; gap: 12px; }\n  .s4 .left { width: 155px; }\n  .s4 .right { flex: 1; }\n  .s4 p { font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.45; margin: 8px 0; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n\n  <!-- ============ HEADER ============ -->\n  <div class=\"header\">\n    <div class=\"nasa-logo\">NASA</div>\n    <div class=\"jpl-text\">\n      <div class=\"l1\">Jet Propulsion Laboratory</div>\n      <div class=\"l2\">California Institute of Technology</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- ============ SECTION 1 ============ -->\n  <section class=\"s1\">\n    <h2>Anatomy of an Active Black Hole</h2>\n\n    <div class=\"stage\">\n      <!-- Host galaxy circle, top right -->\n      <div class=\"placeholder circle\" style=\"position:absolute; right:0px; top:-5px; width:185px; height:185px;\">\n        [Image: host galaxy, bright core — top right]\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"lbl\" style=\"right:8px; top:22px; width:170px;\">\n        <b>Host Galaxy</b><br>\n        <i>Size: about 100,000 light-years</i>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Supermassive black hole circle, left -->\n      <div class=\"placeholder circle\" style=\"position:absolute; left:2px; top:55px; width:205px; height:205px;\">\n        [Image: accretion disk &amp; black hole — left]\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"lbl\" style=\"left:8px; top:70px; width:192px;\">\n        <b>Supermassive Black Hole</b><br>\n        <i>Size: as big as Mercury's orbit</i>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Doughnut circle, center -->\n      <div class=\"placeholder circle\" style=\"position:absolute; left:210px; top:130px; width:165px; height:165px;\">\n        [Image: dusty torus with jets — center]\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"lbl\" style=\"left:212px; top:255px; width:162px;\">\n        <b>&ldquo;Doughnut&rdquo;  Ring of Dust &amp; Gas</b><br>\n        <i>Size: around 1 light year</i>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"bottom\" style=\"margin-top:52px;\">\n      <div class=\"caption center\">\n        Astronomers call supermassive black<br>\n        holes and their surrounding disks<br>\n        &ldquo;Active Galactic Nuclei&rdquo; or &ldquo;AGN&rdquo;\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"caption center\">\n        Black holes emit no light, but<br>\n        the glow from the bright<br>\n        material swirling around them<br>\n        can be seen by telescopes.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ============ SECTION 2 ============ -->\n  <section class=\"s2\">\n    <h2>Why Do Active Black Holes Look Different?</h2>\n\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <div class=\"placeholder circle\" style=\"width:190px; height:190px; margin-left:20px;\">\n        [Image: face-on glowing black hole — left]\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"mid\">\n        In some galaxies the<br>\n        black hole regions are<br>\n        <b><i>incredibly bright</i></b>, while in<br>\n        other galaxies they<br>\n        appear <b><i>much darker.</i></b>\n        <br><br>\n        A <b><i>&ldquo;unified model&rdquo;</i></b><br>\n        suggests the angle at<br>\n        which we view them can<br>\n        explain the differences.\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"placeholder circle\" style=\"width:190px; height:190px; margin-right:12px;\">\n        [Image: edge-on dusty doughnut — right]\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"caps\">\n      <div class=\"caption\">\n        Seen face-on, we detect the light from the<br>\n        hot material surrounding the black hole.\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"caption\">\n        When viewed through the edge of the dusty<br>\n        doughnut, the black hole is hidden.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ============ SECTION 3 ============ -->\n  <section class=\"s3\">\n    <h2>What We Expect to See</h2>\n\n    <div class=\"field\">\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:8px;   top:38px;  width:105px; height:60px;\">[edge-on disk]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:100px; top:88px;  width:100px; height:75px;\">[bright galaxy]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:150px; top:0px;   width:105px; height:70px;\">[dark doughnut]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:330px; top:-2px;  width:100px; height:75px;\">[bright galaxy]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:470px; top:8px;   width:105px; height:60px;\">[dark doughnut]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:465px; top:100px; width:110px; height:78px;\">[bright galaxy]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:8px;   top:170px; width:105px; height:60px;\">[dark doughnut]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:130px; top:185px; width:105px; height:62px;\">[dark doughnut]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:225px; top:198px; width:110px; height:62px;\">[bright galaxy]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:355px; top:175px; width:110px; height:70px;\">[bright galaxy]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"position:absolute; left:490px; top:195px; width:95px;  height:55px;\">[dark doughnut]</div>\n\n      <div class=\"textmid\">\n        Galaxies are oriented randomly in the sky so the disks<br>\n        in their centers should be oriented randomly as well.\n        <br><br>\n        Thus we expect to see a random mix of exposed and<br>\n        hidden black holes <b><i>everywhere we look</i></b>.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ============ SECTION 4 ============ -->\n  <section class=\"s4\">\n    <h2>WISE Observations Challenge &ldquo;Unified Model&rdquo;</h2>\n\n    <div class=\"cols\">\n      <div class=\"left\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"width:155px; height:82px;\">[Photo: WISE spacecraft over Earth]</div>\n        <p>\n          Observations with NASA's Wide-<br>\n          field Infrared Survey Explorer<br>\n          reveal that hidden black holes<br>\n          tend to be <b><i>more clumped</i></b><br>\n          <b><i>together</i></b> than exposed ones.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          This violates the &ldquo;unified model,&rdquo;<br>\n          which predicts we should see<br>\n          the same random distribution of<br>\n          dusty doughnuts regardless of<br>\n          how clumped the objects are.\n        </p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"right\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder\" style=\"width:100%; height:200px;\">[Image: purple halos around clumped galaxies on starfield]</div>\n        <p>\n          Strongly clumped galaxies are likely to have larger halos of dark matter (shown<br>\n          artistically here in purple), which might provide a clue about what else besides the<br>\n          doughnuts could be hiding the black holes.\n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
